{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1097893-pact-benefit-reap-aether","id":1097893,"title":"Pact Benefit: Reap aether","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-28T16:04:24-07:00","id":1097893,"title":"Pact Benefit: Reap aether","content":"What if an unchained learnt or attempted to mimic how a changeling pledge can fuel a changeling? For a demon to attempt to feed on the infrastructure that supports pacts rather than requesting a benefit or as much of a benefit as they normally would be granted.Possibly the mortal would still have to offer up details that would normally be used for cover but the demon choses to not utilize them for cover but instead aether. I feel that this could be an interesting approach to take but there must be a limitation or drawback in my eyes. First off I feel that 1 aether would be have a value of 1 on the demon's side of the contract and be able to go up to a maximum of 3 aether. <br /> <br /> The first main drawback I imagine this would have is that a pact made utilizing such a tactic would be a risk of compromise at -1 for each point of aether gained beyond the first. Then its possible that both the pact and the one benefiting from the pact could register to ether senses for the duration of the pact despite not containing aether themselves.<br /> <br /> If this could not be done innately a gadget could be fashioned by a demon who (foolishly) attempts this act. A near field effect of show of power(changeling pledge) could be required for this to be done with the above still applying.<br /> <br /> I like this idea and I'd like to hammer it out to be more so that it could actually be used in a game as an alternate source of aether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T16:54:56-07:00","id":1097902,"title":"","content":"I feel like the thematic notes that Aether runs through makes this ill-advised \u2014 Aether is a byproduct of the processes of an inhuman engine of alien nature, and it tends to warp things to suit the agenda of the God-Machine rather than the symbolic correspondences familiar to humanity. It's not a human fuel, and the closest it gets to being a product of humanity is that the Machine finds purchase in human systems and burns Essence to accomplish Its activities, and even then, It tends to gather that Essence through peculiarities of the world's occult framework rather than simply inspiring memory and emotion.<br /> <br /> Pacts aren't supported by Infrastructure; Covers are effectively internally-maintained Infrastructure run by a demon, but the mechanism of demonic pactwork is explicitly unknown to at least the point where if it does have anything to do with the God-Machine it's not overt enough to produce Aether. Accordingly, if you <i>do</i> intend to work in a means of having a pact operate like a Glamour-tasked changeling pledge, I'd recommend making it a function of a form of Subverted Infrastructure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T17:31:31-07:00","id":1097913,"title":"","content":"It is an assumption the pacts are maintained by infrastructure, I admit that is not directly said. The intent wouldn't be to to use humanity as a source of aether but to subvert the normal benefit of a pact. It basically would be 'if maintained by infrastructure siphon aether instead of maintain cover'. It isn't currently elegant though so I wish to improve it.<br /> <br /> Having it function more like subverted infrastructure to play closer to a changeling's pledge instead of a one of trade would also allow it to almost be quasi-infastructure so I feel that is by far a more interesting idea. The main difference it should have from a changeling pledge and more like subverted infrastructure would a demon would have to gather the gathered aether itself. This brings the interesting idea of another poaching or discovering it like one must worry with suborned infrastructure.I'll have to look into this method more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T18:21:15-07:00","id":1097925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1097893-pact-benefit-reap-aether?p=1097913#post1097913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is an assumption the pacts are maintained by infrastructure, I admit that is not directly said. The intent wouldn't be to to use humanity as a source of aether but to subvert the normal benefit of a pact. It basically would be 'if maintained by infrastructure siphon aether instead of maintain cover'. It isn't currently elegant though so I wish to improve it.<br /> <br /> Having it function more like subverted infrastructure to play closer to a changeling's pledge instead of a one of trade would also allow it to almost be quasi-infastructure so I feel that is by far a more interesting idea. The main difference it should have from a changeling pledge and more like subverted infrastructure would a demon would have to gather the gathered aether itself. This brings the interesting idea of another poaching or discovering it like one must worry with suborned infrastructure.I'll have to look into this method more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Easiest method would be turning the pact or the pacted away whatever into Suborned Infrastructure.<br /> <br /> Either the document starts radiating Aether and is ideal for theft, or say you are pacting for an abusive girlfriend, that girlfriend becomes defuct, Aether-leaking Infrastructure. Collection would be handling the document, or interaction with the girlfriend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-28-2017, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T18:41:54-07:00","id":1097928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1097893-pact-benefit-reap-aether?p=1097925#post1097925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Easiest method would be turning the pact or the pacted away whatever into Suborned Infrastructure.<br /> <br /> Either the document starts radiating Aether and is ideal for theft, or say you are pacting for an abusive girlfriend, that girlfriend becomes defuct, Aether-leaking Infrastructure. Collection would be handling the document, or interaction with the girlfriend.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that the pacted would be more suitable to act as the suborned infrastructure. It would be too easy to simply secure the document in comparison and this would bring it closer to the suborned infrastructure. Though I feel it may fit better to be focused on the one who is bound by the pact and benefits rather than the 'sold' or 'bought' variable.<br /> <br /> But yes, making it simply function like suborned infrastructure may be the easiest and best approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T19:50:18-07:00","id":1097943,"title":"","content":"I should clarify that I wasn't suggesting &quot;make some element of the pact act as the Suborned Infrastructure Merit&quot; so much as &quot;make this effect a function of hacking the Machine that makes use of Suborned Infrastructure&quot; \u2014 my highlighting the lack of direct sources of Aether in humanity was intended to bridge to &quot;so if you want to use pacts to get Aether you're going to need something that actually produces Aether involved at some point,&quot; not &quot;so using pacts to get Aether should <i>spontaneously generate sources of Aether</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> Plugging the documentation into the Infrastructure's processes somewhere and rolling for compromise to generate Aether upon fulfillment of the task seems the most immediate means of accomplishing the desired outcome, but I'm sure there are other suitably evocative routes to take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-28-2017, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T04:35:09-07:00","id":1098062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1097893-pact-benefit-reap-aether?p=1097943#post1097943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should clarify that I wasn't suggesting &quot;make some element of the pact act as the Suborned Infrastructure Merit&quot; so much as &quot;make this effect a function of hacking the Machine that makes use of Suborned Infrastructure&quot; \u2014 my highlighting the lack of direct sources of Aether in humanity was intended to bridge to &quot;so if you want to use pacts to get Aether you're going to need something that actually produces Aether involved at some point,&quot; not &quot;so using pacts to get Aether should <i>spontaneously generate sources of Aether</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> Plugging the documentation into the Infrastructure's processes somewhere and rolling for compromise to generate Aether upon fulfillment of the task seems the most immediate means of accomplishing the desired outcome, but I'm sure there are other suitably evocative routes to take.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> \u200bI think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2909_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2909\" data-vbnamecard=\"2909\">Mr.F.I.X.</a> is looking at Pacting <i>itself</i> as utilizing Infrastructure that Demons have inherently used/Suborned in order to make the whole thing work at all. In this case, it just changes the Output from Concealment (maintain a piece of Cover) to Logistics (generate resource - in this case, Aether byproduct).<br /> <br /> Plugging a Pact Document into existing Infrastructure for Aether generation seems less or counter-productive - if you already have access to it to that degree, why not just Suborn that Infrastructure and keep the Pact for Cover purposes? I suppose an argument might be made for relative difficulty regarding either action, but that is a bit specific for each case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T13:57:47-07:00","id":1098227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1097893-pact-benefit-reap-aether?p=1098062#post1098062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2909_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2909\" data-vbnamecard=\"2909\">Mr.F.I.X.</a> is looking at Pacting <i>itself</i> as utilizing Infrastructure that Demons have inherently used/Suborned in order to make the whole thing work at all. In this case, it just changes the Output from Concealment (maintain a piece of Cover) to Logistics (generate resource - in this case, Aether byproduct).</div> </div> </div> </div>Suborned Infrastructure operates by reconfiguring Infrastructure that actually does something into an infinite loop that prevents it from reaching the Output stage while still generating paranormal waste heat.<br /> <br /> Siphoning Aether from Infrastructure itself needs a concrete linkup that's usually confined to a single exhaust valve; if the overall functioning of pacts <i>is</i> maintained by Infrastructure, it shouldn't be any more suitable to harvesting than the hypothetical linguistic exploits hidden in the Shadow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plugging a Pact Document into existing Infrastructure for Aether generation seems less or counter-productive - if you already have access to it to that degree, why not just Suborn that Infrastructure and keep the Pact for Cover purposes? </div> </div> </div>For much the same reason that I don't spend time and money buying studio tickets to my local radio station instead of getting a car radio: voodoo-dolling the Aether into my Primum through a document that has an inherent connection to me and is a security risk anyway stands a better chance of going undetected than regularly visiting the location in person.<br /> <br /> In any case, the bit of Changeling 1e pledgecraft that serves as the basis for this idea runs on two things, one of which is not comparable to demonic pactwork:<br /> <br /> 1. Upholding an oath grants the character a point of the resource tied to the energies of Arcadia, which is bound up in the Wyrd as a thing that cares about promises.<br /> <br /> 2. As part of a pledge, a Glamour boon exists in a framework where the other party has also agreed to a task.<br /> <br /> Given that Demon's metaphysics involve rather more concrete resources than Changeling's do, using a pact with a mortal to generate actual Aether (instead of plain Aetheric resonance like a bill of sale) should involve more significant interference than leaving a saucer of milk out when the shoes are fixed \u2014 the most subtle channel that seems viable to me is &quot;the mortal agrees to mess with a piece of Infrastructure and/or tap it for Aether, allowing the pact to channel the resource from the mortal to the demon.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}